            <ArticleTitle>Intracardiac leiomyomatosis: iliac vein to right-ventricular outflow tract.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>369-72; quiz 373</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">A 58-year-old female with a history of hypertension and asthma presented to an internist for a routine physical examination. A grade II/VI systolic ejection murmur and electrocardiogram abnormalities were noted. She was referred to a cardiologist for further assessment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INVESTIGATIONS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Transthoracic echocardiography, transesophageal echocardiography, contrast-enhanced CT and MRI, exploratory laparotomy.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DIAGNOSIS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Intracardiac leiomyomatosis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MANAGEMENT" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Surgical excision.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
